# Function rules

Har naya function isi pattern pe likho.

## Returns (JS)

- PHP Sonar single-return yahan apply mat karo. JS me **early return / guard clause** use karo.
- DB/cache helpers (`getUserDetails`, `getAdminAuthUser`) fail pe **`null`**. `{}` / partial mat return karo.
- `null` cache mat karo. Cache sirf complete valid object.

```js
const doWork = async (id) => {
  const row = await find(id);
  if (!row || row.status !== 1) return null;

  const result = { id: row.id, name: row.name };
  cacheSet(key, result);
  return result;
};
```

## API response

- Envelope: `{ status, message?, data?, error_code? }`. `success` field mat use karo.
- **`status` number hai, boolean nahi** — taaki baad me `2`, `3`, `4` bhi bhej sako.
  - Fail: `status: 0` (+ `error_code`, `message`)
  - Success: `status: 1` (+ optional `message`, `data`)
  - Future: `2+` reserved
- Fail: `errorResponse(key, data?)` → `{ status: 0, error_code, message, data? }`
- Success: `successResponse(data, message?)` → `{ status: 1, message?, data? }`. Success pe `error_code` nahi.
- Codes sirf `constants.mjs` `MESSAGE_CODES` + `getMessageCode(key)` / `errorResponse(key)`. File me `"100001"` string mat likho.
- Ranges: auth `10xxxx`, users `20xxxx`, orgs `30xxxx`. Same meaning = same `key`.
- `res.status(401).json(errorResponse("AUTH_TOKEN_MISSING"))` — HTTP code alag; body `status` number alag. DB `user.status` se mix mat karo.
- Controllers hamesha `res.status(...).json(...)` — bare `return errorResponse(...)` mat.
- DB/cache helpers fail pe **`null`**, envelope nahi.

## Permissions (`can`)

- Helper: `can(userOrKeys, permission)` — call: `can(req.authUser, "organization.view")`.
- Super Admin (unrestricted `role_type`) → hamesha `true` (permission table se nahi).
- Staff → `user.permissions` me slug / `*` check. Nested: `user.role?.role_type` bhi padho.
- Array of keys bhi: `can(["organization.view"], "organization.view")`.
- `requirePermission` thin middleware; gate `can(...)` se.

## Cache

- Keys: `user:{id}`, `organization:{id}`, `membership:{userId}:{orgId}`, `admin_auth:{userId}`, `auth:{userId}:{orgId|platform}`.
- Cache **id / membership pair** par. `findAll` / search / filter cache mat karo.
- Sequelize list pe `order` use karo, `orderBy` nahi.
- User/role/permission/membership update par related keys delete (`cacheDel` / `cacheDelByPrefix`).
- Memory `Map` abhi theek; Redis baad me — key names mat badalna.

## Constants

- Shared values sirf root `constants.mjs`.
- Ek array: `{ key, value, label, badgeClass?, panel? }` + `getX(key)` helper. Duplicate object mat banao.
- Customer `ROLE_TYPE_CODES` me nahi. Super Admin permission table se nahi — gate `role_type` / `can()` se.

## Auth middleware

- `AdminAuth` = platform panel. Sirf `panel === "admin"` (`SUPER_ADMIN` + `SUPER_ADMIN_STAFF`).
- Token verify → `adminAuthValidate` → `req.authUser`. Email Super Admin check nahi — `role_type` se.
- JWT: `{ user_id }`. `adminAuthValidate` me token mat banao — token sirf login pe.
- Fail body: `errorResponse("AUTH_...")` from `constants.mjs`.
